+// sand path, a stone castle wall and a wooden bridge in the same level would all dig like grass.
+// The level's own display lists know better: each visible triangle has a texture. This file looks
+// at the level's visible triangles once per area (their texture's average colour, tinted by their
+// vertex colours), and for each collision triangle finds the visible surface it covers and turns
+// that colour into a Minecraft material: green grass, yellow sand, brown dirt, grey stone, white
+// snow, red bricks...
